msgstr "Concrete types such as Vertices provide singular-reference iteration and bulk operations. They share the Shape wrapper and fix the index sequence at construction. Indices do not automatically follow geometry additions or deletions, and element identity after topology changes is not guaranteed. Brackets address positions within the stored sequence, not actual Maya indices."

